==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|laff}} {{qualifier|eye dialect}}
* {{l|en|laughe}} {{qualifier|archaic}}
* {{l|en|larf}} {{qualifier|[[Cockney]] eye dialect}}

===Etymology===
{{wikipedia}}
From {{inh|en|enm|laughen}}, {{m|enm|laghen}}, from (Anglian) {{inh|en|ang|hlæhhan}}, {{m|ang|hlehhan}}, (West Saxon) {{m|ang|hliehhan}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hlahhjan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hlahjaną}}.
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Germanic: (with ''j''-present) {{cog|sco|lauch}}, {{cog|is|hlæja}}, {{cog|no|-}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|da|le}}; (without) Low German {{m|nds-de|lachen}}, {{cog|nl|lachen}}, {{cog|de|lachen}}.

Indo-European: Russian {{m|ru|клекота́ть}}, {{m|ru|клокота́ть}}, {{m|ru|клохта́ть}} ‘to cluck, cackle’, {{cog|grc|κλώζω}}, {{m|grc|κλώσσω}} ‘to cackle, clack’, {{cog|cy|cloch}} ‘bell’, possibly {{cog|la|glōcīre}} ‘to cluck’.
{{rel-bottom}}

